---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import {places,regions} from '../../lib/regions';
import '../../styles/regions.css';
---
<Site title="Places & Perspectives" active="Stories"><header class="wrap page-head regional-header"><a href="/stories/">Stories &amp; journeys</a><p class="kicker">LOCAL HISTORIES · DIFFERENT PERSPECTIVES</p><h1>Places &amp;<br/><em>Perspectives</em></h1><p class="lead">Begin with a town. Follow a record. Let each place keep its own history.</p><p class="regional-status">Research drafts · private review only · public release not granted</p></header>
<section class="wrap section place-grid" aria-label="Town-specific readings">{places.map(p=><article class="place-card" id={p.id}><p class="kicker">{p.storyId?'DOCUMENTARY STORY PILOT':'PRESERVED ARCHIVE READING'}</p><h2 lang="yo">{p.name}</h2><p>{p.context}</p>{p.storyId&&regions.filter(s=>s.id===p.storyId).map(s=><a class="place-story-link" href={`/places/${s.id}/`}>{s.title}</a>)}<a href={`/articles/${p.articleId}/#section-${p.section}`}>Read the original {p.name} section</a><p class="fine">{p.storyId?'New story awaits independent editorial, community, language and rights review.':'Original research draft; this link does not imply newly verified history.'}</p></article>)}</section>
<figure class="wrap regional-figure"><img src="/editorial/representation-reading.svg" width="1200" height="600" alt="Three conceptual reading questions: who proposes a charge, who is represented, and who approves it. This is not a historical institutional diagram."/><figcaption>Original conceptual illustration. No historical map, building, person or constitutional procedure is reconstructed.</figcaption></figure>
<aside class="wrap notice"><h2>A place name is not a source.</h2><p>Regional accuracy requires a named record and a clear scope. The new Abẹ́òkúta reading follows selected documents; the Ìbàdàn link returns to the preserved library. No new origin story or authenticated oral testimony is claimed.</p><a href="/articles/know-governance/#section-1">Explore the original governance research draft</a></aside></Site>
